  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Ge tribe Gu Masters watching Fang Yuan under the Chang Shan Yin name class his wolf control with Jiang Bao Ya, Yang Po Ying, and Ma Zun as first-rate Northern Plains enslavement skill, and they treat those three as holders of thousand man souls.",
      "chapters": [
        438
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ge_tribe",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_chang_shan_yin",
        "char_jiang_bao_ya",
        "char_ma_zun",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan weighs northern plains beast groups and places Yang Po Ying with Ma Zun and Jiang Bao Ya among the masters whose herds run to hundreds of thousands, at least four hundred thousand in one of his counts, with a mutated thunder eagle group as trump card.",
      "chapters": [
        482
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "thunder-eagle-group",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Nu Er Tu joins the enslavement master ranks after beating Jiang Bao Ya, talk groups Jiang Bao Ya, Yang Po Ying, Ma Zun, Chang Shan Yin, and Nu Er Tu as five beast kings, and Eagle King Yang Po Ying is the one with the mutated thunder eagle group.",
      "chapters": [
        525
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "thunder-eagle-group",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_nu_er_tu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ma Ying Jie treats Rat King’s move into Yang tribe as an alliance of Rat King and Eagle King Yang Po Ying that briefly lifts that underdog tribe in the Imperial Court struggle, while still calling Yang tribe foundations far inferior to Ma tribe and Rat King already crippled.",
      "chapters": [
        529
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yang-tribe-then-ma-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_ying_jie",
        "fac_yang_tribe",
        "loc_imperial_court",
        "fac_ma_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Ma tribe defeats Ye Lui tribe and absorbs Yang tribe among other forces, Ma Shang Feng’s side fields Yang Po Ying with Jiang Bao Ya and Ma Zun as three enslavement path masters against Hei Lou Lan.",
      "chapters": [
        539
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "yang-tribe-then-ma-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ye_lui_tribe",
        "char_ma_shang_feng",
        "char_hei_lou_lan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In that three-group charge Horse King Ma Zun, Rat King Jiang Bao Ya, and Eagle King Yang Po Ying move together. Yang Po Ying rides a huge eagle, challenges Wolf King by name, and tries to pin Fang Yuan’s wolves from the air while Rat King mocks and Ma Zun charges with horse-guard experts.",
      "chapters": [
        539
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "challenge-on-the-battlefield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan later floods the field with over a million wolves, Yang Po Ying’s battle intent freezes with the others; with horse and rat groups already cut off or fleeing, he chooses to restrain Wolf King rather than abandon the Gu Master lines, then sends Wu Ye and other fliers to press the experts around Fang Yuan while claiming thunder eagle cover keeps him safe.",
      "chapters": [
        540
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "challenge-on-the-battlefield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "char_wu_ye"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After killing Cheng Hu, Fang Yuan flies straight at Yang Po Ying. Yang Po Ying pulls the thunder eagle group in for cover, but Fang Yuan smashes through those beasts of rank four battle strength, lifts him by the head, and bursts Eagle King Yang Po Ying’s skull. The eagle group crumbles and flees into the sky as the battlefield names the kill.",
      "chapters": [
        541
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_cheng_hu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes the name as Yang Po Ying and the title Eagle King Yang Po Ying. One line in chapter 540 uses a feminine pronoun for him while the surrounding narration keeps masculine forms; this page follows the majority usage. No Chinese characters for the personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
